# switch-lm

Nintendo Switch homebrew (libnx) for running language models on the console.

## Dev environment setup

PLEASE NOTE THIS SECTION IS SLOPPED BY AI AND HAS NOT BEEN TESTED ON ANOTHER MACHINE

### Requirements

- **macOS** (Intel or Apple Silicon) or **Debian/Ubuntu Linux**. These can be set up automatically.
- Other platforms (Windows, Arch, Fedora…) need devkitPro installed by hand first. See
  [devkitPro pacman](https://devkitpro.org/wiki/devkitPro_pacman), then run the setup script below.
- `git`, `curl`, and `sudo` access. On macOS, [Homebrew](https://brew.sh) is used for host tools.

### One-time setup

```sh
git clone <repo-url> switch-lm
cd switch-lm
make setup        # same as: scripts/setup.sh
```

`make setup` is safe to re-run. It skips anything already installed. It will:

1. Install **devkitPro pacman** (`dkp-pacman`) if missing, using the official installer
   (a `.pkg` on macOS, the apt.devkitpro.org script on Debian/Ubuntu).
2. Install the devkitPro packages listed in [`dkp-packages.txt`](dkp-packages.txt), the
   authoritative list (if you add a package, add it there):
   - **Toolchain and SDK:** `switch-dev` (which includes `devkitA64`, `libnx`, `switch-tools`)
   - **UI:** `switch-sdl2`, `switch-sdl2_ttf`
   - **GPU:** `deko3d`, `uam` (shader compiler)
   - **Build and debug:** `switch-cmake` (for cross-compiling llama.cpp), `devkitA64-gdb`
3. Check the `DEVKITPRO` environment variable.
4. Install host tools if missing: `cmake`, `clang-format`.
5. Turn on the repo's git hooks (`git config core.hooksPath .githooks`).

Then add this line to your `~/.zshrc` (or `~/.bashrc`) and open a new terminal:

```sh
export DEVKITPRO=/opt/devkitpro
```

The Makefiles fall back to `/opt/devkitpro` if this isn't set, but other tools (CMake, VS Code) expect it.

### Check your environment

```sh
make doctor       # same as: scripts/setup.sh --check — reports only, changes nothing
```

It warns if an installed package version differs from the one in `dkp-packages.txt` (the versions
this project was last tested with). devkitPro only serves the latest packages, so a different
version usually still works.

### Editor (VS Code)

Install the **C/C++** extension (`ms-vscode.cpptools`). Open the **repo root** as the workspace.
IntelliSense is preconfigured in `.vscode/c_cpp_properties.json` with the
**DKP aarch64** configuration. If `#include <switch.h>` shows an error:

- pick **DKP aarch64** in the status bar,
- run **C/C++: Change Configuration Provider → None** (CMake Tools can take over IntelliSense),
- then run **Developer: Reload Window**.

> The config uses `/opt/devkitpro` paths. On Windows, change them to `C:/devkitPro/...`.

## Building and running

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make` | Builds `switch-lm/switch-lm.nro` |
| `make run` | Builds, then sends the `.nro` to the Switch over Wi-Fi and shows its output in your terminal |
| `make run SWITCH_IP=192.168.1.50` | Same, if the Switch isn't found automatically |
| `make clean` | Removes build outputs |

**Running on the Switch** (needs Atmosphère + hbmenu):

- **Over Wi-Fi:** open hbmenu, press **Y** (netloader), then `make run`.
- **From the SD card:** copy `switch-lm/switch-lm.nro` to `SD:/switch/`. Launch hbmenu by **holding R while starting any game** (this gives the app full memory), then pick switch-lm.

## Git hooks

The pre-commit hook (`.githooks/pre-commit`) checks only the files you're committing. It blocks:

- build outputs and model files (`.nro`, `.elf`, `.nacp`, `.dksh`, `.gguf`, `.o`, `.a`, `build/`),
- files larger than 1 MB,
- leftover merge-conflict markers and trailing whitespace,
- C/C++ files that don't match `.clang-format`. This check is skipped if `clang-format` isn't installed.
  Fix with `clang-format -i <files>`.

To skip it once in an emergency: `git commit --no-verify`.

## Project layout

```
.
├── Makefile             # top-level shortcuts: setup / doctor / build / run / clean
├── dkp-packages.txt     # devkitPro package manifest
├── scripts/setup.sh     # dev environment installer / checker
├── .githooks/           # git hooks (pre-commit)
├── .clang-format        # C/C++ style
└── switch-lm/           # the homebrew app
    ├── Makefile         # libnx build (based on the devkitPro template)
    └── source/          # app source code
```

---

## App Makefile reference (`switch-lm/Makefile`)

### Makefile variables

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `TARGET` | Name of the output |
| `BUILD` | Directory where object files and intermediate files go |
| `SOURCES` | Directories containing source code |
| `DATA` | Directories containing data files |
| `INCLUDES` | Directories containing header files |
| `ROMFS` | Directory of data added to RomFS, relative to the Makefile *(optional)* |

### Flags

| Flag | Effect |
|---|---|
| `NO_ICON` | If set to anything, no icon is used |
| `NO_NACP` | If set to anything, no `.nacp` file is generated |

### NACP metadata (all optional)

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `APP_TITLE` | App name stored in the `.nacp` |
| `APP_AUTHOR` | App author stored in the `.nacp` |
| `APP_VERSION` | App version stored in the `.nacp` |
| `APP_TITLEID` | Title ID stored in the `.nacp` |

### Icon

`ICON` is the icon's filename (`.jpg`), relative to the project folder. If it's not set, the build tries these in order:

1. `<Project name>.jpg`
2. `icon.jpg`
3. `<libnx folder>/default_icon.jpg`
